# tactics-own: built from Kepler-64's own ladder games against Stockfish 19 (gen-002 vs a strength-limited Stockfish).
# Stockfish (Stockfish 19) was used only as the examiner, to verify each position. The suite is for measurement only and is never used for training.
# source: 50 game files in results/ladder-gen002 (1000 games, 76780 distinct candidate positions from ply 10 on, both sides to move): m-1320-0.json .. m-2100-9.json
# kept when Stockfish (MultiPV 2, depth 16, Threads 4, Hash 64) scores the best move in [+200, +600] cp for the side to move, not a mate-in-1,
# and the second-best move is at least 200 cp worse (a unique winning move); positions with fewer than 2 legal moves skipped; deduplicated by FEN (first four fields); at most 2 per game.
# selection: candidates shuffled with seed 1, examined in that order until 200 were kept (12490 examined, 1071 passed the depth-8 pre-screen with relaxed thresholds [+100, +900] cp and gap 100; thresholds below decide).
# command: kepler-train suite-build-tactics --games results/ladder-gen002 --count 200 --seed 1 --sf-depth 16 --sf-threads 4 --pre-depth 8 --min-ply 10 --per-game 2 --out data/suites/tactics-own.epd; built 2026-10-24
